    "done_when": "The the-suite-is-green-at-head followup f-sgh-basetemp-lock-is-exact holds. tests/conftest.py records the lock holder's process start time (field 22 of the holder process stat file under /proc) beside its pid, and treats a lock whose pid is alive but whose recorded start time differs from that pid's current start time as stale, so it is taken over. acquire_basetemp_lock writes the lock content to a temporary sibling file and links it into place with os.link, so the lock path never exists without its holder's pid and start time; a lock file read as empty or unparseable is refused while it is younger than five seconds rather than unlinked. docs/evidence/fragments/the-suite-is-green-at-head/a-shared-basetemp-is-refused.html names 2225ab398 as the head arm's revision. tests/test_a_shared_basetemp_is_refused.py gains two cases: a lock naming a live pid with a different recorded start time is taken over, and a second session started while the first's lock holds only a partial write is refused. Each new case is red under a declared negative control executed and logged under pytest: comparing pid alone reddens the reuse case, and creating the lock with O_EXCL then writing reddens the partial-write case. The node gate is tests/test_a_shared_basetemp_is_refused.py at head under pytest -n 8 with its own --basetemp under $TMPDIR, ending EXIT=0. Every log sits under the run directory, headed with revision, tree and literal command, and ends EXIT=. Only tests/conftest.py, tests/test_a_shared_basetemp_is_refused.py and that evidence fragment change.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "make the basetemp lock refuse only a live holder of the same process",
